#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317515 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101023 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "41bedcde-cbc1-5634-8846-eb58ffda32e2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Interval Given the Average Value of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c20d1097-852b-5f82-8d60-8924f36cf4a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316208}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c20d1097-852b-5f82-8d60-8924f36cf4a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316208} :answer-field/id #uuid "357cc33c-157b-5cf7-bef4-4852d1fed751" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316672}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9972073a-20c3-5456-964a-3f9b441520bb" :question/math-academy-id "q-344601" :question/problem "The **exact** value of $c$ such that the average value of $f(x)=-15\\sqrt{x}+6$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $-4$ is\n\n$c=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -4 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}{\\int }_{0}^{c}(-15\\sqrt{x}+6)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -4 & ={\\frac{1}{c}(-10{x}^{3/2}+6x)|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ -4 & =\\frac{1}{c}[(-10{c}^{3/2}+6c)-0] \\\\ -4 & =-10\\sqrt{c}+6 \\\\ -10 & =-10\\sqrt{c} \\\\ 1 & =\\sqrt{c} \\\\ c & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $c$ is \n\n$$\nc=1.\n$$"}]}
